    "created_at": "2017-03-09T14:24:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-09T14:24:40Z",
    "body": "The reason for that is security -- exposing network error reason to JS would be exposing new information that could be used as part of an attack. Browsers can log information in their developer tools, though. If browsers don't do that now and you would like them to, I recommend filing browser bugs requesting that.\r\n\r\nClosing this but happy to continue discussing in the closed issue. We can reopen if there is something we can expose to JS that would not be a potential security vector.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
