    "created_at": "2017-03-09T23:37:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-09T23:37:39Z",
    "body": "OK. I understand you think you ran into OOM. The problem with OOM though is that it's difficult to require any specific behavior, as the user agent might not be able to do that in the face of OOM. I'm also not aware of any other part of the web platform that deals with OOM, other than this catch-all:\r\n\r\n> User agents may impose implementation-specific limits on otherwise unconstrained inputs, e.g. to prevent denial of service attacks, to guard against running out of memory, or to work around platform-specific limitations.\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#conformance-classes",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
